---
/*
  The real blocker of the most valuable group is the old agency, not the price.
  04-konzept.md section 4.3, page "/switching".
  Hard limit that has to stay in the copy: reading and sorting a contract is
  not legal advice. Same logic as the ban on tax and banking statements in
  appendix A of the closing playbook.
  Sprache: einfaches Englisch, Ansage Manuel 07.09.2026 abends.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Switching agencies | Wunder"
  description="What happens when you are still signed with another agency, in what order, and where our help stops."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Leaving an agency you signed with.</h1>
      <p class="lead">This is the part most people are stuck on. It is not the money.</p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>I am so nervous about telling my other agency. You have no idea.</p>
        <p class="caption">
          A line we hear a lot in these talks. Not a quote from a client, and no name on it.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What we do.</h2>
      <p>
        Send us your deal and we read it with you. We tell you how much notice you owe. We tell you
        when your next way out opens. We tell you what the part about your content means in real
        life.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is reading and sorting. It is not legal advice. We are not lawyers, and we are not
        yours. When a paper needs a lawyer, we say so. Then you take it to one.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not call your agency. We do not write to them in your name. We do not ask you to
        break a deal you signed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The order things happen in.</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>You apply. In the form you say that you are still tied, and until when.</li>
        <li>We talk anyway. That call ties you to nothing.</li>
        <li>We read your deal. We work out the first clean date you can leave.</li>
        <li>
          You give notice yourself, in writing, in the window your deal allows. We do not start
          before that date.
        </li>
        <li>
          We start after your old deal ends. On day one we read your last thirty days. That is
          your starting point.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Maybe your deal has no clean way out for months. Then we say so. We put a date in the
        calendar instead of talking you into something.
      </p>
      <CtaBlock secondary />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  blockquote {
    margin: 32px 0 0;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  blockquote p:first-child {
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  blockquote p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
